<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3351" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăraxes</span></b> , is,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀράξης</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Armenia Major</i>, now <i>Aras</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8, 728</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 4,
				11, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Hippol. 47</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 9,
				9, § 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 5,
				5</span></i>.—<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a dweller on the Araxes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pharetratus Araxes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 5, 2, 32</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in Persia</i>, now <i>Bendemir</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 4, 5, 21</span></i>. 
			</div>
